invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: the signer includes rsa_ifma.h, the first step to a call into the
  AVX-512 IFMA kernel, which takes public input alone: the compiler keeps
  its 512-bit registers in stack slots that no wipe can name, and the
  signer's operands are secret. The script requires that no root source
  but rsa_mont.c includes rsa_ifma.h or calls into it.

--- old
#include "ch_assert.h"
#include "ct.h"

// The bits of the exponent one step reads
--- new
#include "ch_assert.h"
#include "ct.h"
#include "rsa_ifma.h"

// The bits of the exponent one step reads
